# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Another project's business — never Habeas's.
#
# Habeas publishes ITS OWN contract: the record shape (docs/RECORD-CONTRACT.md)
# and the integration API (docs/external-hooks.md, docs/INTEGRATION.md). How any
# particular consumer ingests that — its endpoint, its model mapping, its
# roadmap, its progress — belongs to that project's repository, not this one.
# A consumer's notes living here make Habeas look like it serves one of them,
# and they rot, because nobody who can correct them is reading this repo.
#
# Kept deliberately broad: the point is that NOTHING consumer-specific is
# committed again, not that these particular filenames stay out.
consumers/
*-progress.md
*-progress-*.md
*-progress.html
*-data-contract.md

# Working notes about real accounts — and docs/ is the PUBLISHED web root.
#
# docs/incidencias/ holds incident write-ups and the captures behind them: real
# transaction ids, real amounts, real dates from somebody's bank. Committing them
# would not merely put them in the repository, it would SERVE them at
# habeas.dev/incidencias/, because GitHub Pages publishes this directory.
#
# The PII guard caught this once, on a long digit run. It must not be the only
# thing standing between a capture and the open web: a capture with no long
# numbers in it would have gone straight through.
docs/incidencias/

